# Time-boxed exception for the Rasta service image scans (ci.yml job
# `containers`, step "Scan image"). It mirrors, and must be deleted together
# with, the `auditConfig.ignoreGhsas` entry for GHSA-mrhx-c7xc-m3w5 in
# pnpm-workspace.yaml (#373), where the reasoning is recorded in full.
#
# CVE-2023-54404 is the same advisory as GHSA-mrhx-c7xc-m3w5 (zod <4.6.6,
# memory exhaustion while validating an oversized array). Trivy's database
# started reporting it against the zod 3.25.76 inside every service image on
# 2026-10-24; the dependency audit has ignored it since 2026-10-23. The only
# fix is the zod 4 migration (W#1 task 087), not an override. Reached at
# runtime, bounded by each service's JSON body limit (16 kb to 512 kb).
# Expires on its own: on 2026-10-30, the same re-check date as the audit
# entry, every service image scan fails again unless the migration has
# merged (delete this file) or the exception is re-reviewed.
CVE-2023-54404 exp:2026-10-30
